    "summary": "A mostly hairless perennial flowering plant predominantly native to western Europe, heath lobelia also occurs in northern Morocco and Madeira. It has shiny, toothed dark-green leaves and blue-purple flowers from May to September. It favours seasonally waterlogged, acidic ground in grassy heaths, rough pastures and open woodland.",
