    "taxonId": 465622,
    "summary": "A subtropical succulent native to the arid Karoo of South Africa’s Eastern Cape, Euphorbia obesa is a thornless, ball-shaped plant. It usually has eight ridges and grey-green skin marked with lighter or darker horizontal stripes, sometimes developing red and purple areas in direct sunlight. Its latex is toxic.",
