    "taxonId": 167724,
    "summary": "A perennial flowering herb native to northern North America, small yellow water-crowfoot is also present in Eurasia. It grows with creeping stems on moist ground or floating stems in shallow water, bearing divided round or kidney-shaped leaves and yellow flowers.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
