    "taxonId": 78338,
    "summary": "An annual grass native to much of the eastern United States and parts of Canada, Panicum dichotomiflorum also occurs in the western United States, where it may be introduced in some climates. Its hairless leaves distinguish it from witchgrass, and it bears a large, open, spreading flower cluster. It grows in sunny, moist habitats and flowers from midsummer through autumn.",
